%chk=probe_h2o_nowindow.chk
%mem=2GB
%nprocshared=1
#P HF/STO-3G NoSymm Int=NoBasisTransform SCF=(Conver=10)
# Output=MatrixElement Tran=Full

probe_h2o_nowindow: the control. Identical to probe_h2o_rhf in every way except
that Window=(2,7) is absent, so the transformation should cover all 7 MOs.

THE POINT OF THIS JOB is that it is the only way to prove Window= is doing
anything. If this one reports a 7^4 = 2401 two-electron block and probe_h2o_rhf
reports 6^4 = 1296, the keyword works and the whole method rests on solid
ground. If both come back the same size, Window= was silently ignored, the
"never transform the full MO space" claim is false, and the route needs fixing
before any of the other results mean anything.

Diff the two probe JSON reports against each other; that comparison is the
actual deliverable of this job.

0 1
O   0.0000000   0.0000000   0.1173000
H   0.0000000   0.7572000  -0.4692000
